      "message": "\u003e add PLATFORM_EC_HOSTCMD_I2C_CONTROL\n\u003e (sorry, i had a typo in the bug comment)\n\nI assume we anyway need to enable `CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_CONSOLE_CMD_I2C_SPEED` kconfig to able to control the i2c speed using EC console. I could see the Nissa (other Zephyr project) device has this kconfig enabled.\n\nAdditionally, `PLATFORM_EC_HOSTCMD_I2C_CONTROL` seems only enabled for `herobrine` device and Nissa is not even enabled this kconfig. What do you suggest in this case? @caveh@chromium.org/@scott?\n\ngrep -rsn \"PLATFORM_EC_HOSTCMD_I2C_CONTROL\" .\n./zephyr/shim/include/config_chip.h:235:#ifdef CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_HOSTCMD_I2C_CONTROL\n./zephyr/projects/herobrine/prj.conf:21:CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_HOSTCMD_I2C_CONTROL\u003dy\n./zephyr/Kconfig.i2c:56:config PLATFORM_EC_HOSTCMD_I2C_CONTROL\n./zephyr/Kconfig.tcpm:126:  imply PLATFORM_EC_HOSTCMD_I2C_CONTROL",
